content:
@Oced Khan ☠, I get where you are coming from in the foundation-room chat (and no worries about English, lots of international ppl here, so we all should give ppl some grace since it's not their mother tongue)! I think the interesting thing about this market is that, like the free market in the real world, people can pay whatever they want, for whatever they want. To the point that JayWalk brought up, no one can say something isn't worth a certain amount. We all are in different situations and make different decisions. That is the beauty of this market.

I believe that one of your points is people who don't know (or didn't read) about claim stake drops (mining drill and power plant) might have an issue. That is indeed going to be a risk perpetually (there will always be mechanics that people can game). As we move forward and go to a broader audience, I think most people would be in agreement that we (community and SA team) all need to do a better job of having things well-documented and very clear. That being said, for this current sale, the majority of buyers will be ones from the project already and so familiar with the limitations.

I definitely think the spirit of your concern is valid, and we just hope that the impact is limited since most buyers will already be familiar.
